diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..afa360f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,127 @@
+# Quizzy
+
+A Rust/SQLite app for preparing conference quizzes, using the supplied Quizzy
+mockups and local Inter font. Moderator pages live at `/moderate` and use HTTP
+Basic authentication. No external services or CDN assets are used.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+export PORT=3000
+export SECRET_KEY_BASE='replace-with-a-long-random-secret'
+export QUIZZY_MODERATOR_USERNAME='moderator'
+export QUIZZY_MODERATOR_PASSWORD='replace-with-your-password'
+bin/serve
+```
+
+The launcher builds the locked dependencies **offline in release mode**, creates
+`storage/` and initializes SQLite, then runs in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:$PORT`.
+`GET /up` returns 200 once startup is complete. Data is stored in
+`storage/quizzy.sqlite3`; stop the app before copying the whole storage directory
+for a backup, or use SQLite's backup command while it is running.
+
+Quizzes support question ordering, immediately saved Active checkboxes, multiple
+correct options, and native delete confirmations. Preview is single-choice and
+uses only active questions; answers and scores exist only in page memory.
+
+## Play live
+
+Open a quiz and choose **Start a game**. Share the full join URL or its QR code
+with the room. Players enter **Your name** and **Join**, without accounts.
+
+Use **Start**, **Finish**, **Next**, and finally **End quiz** on the moderator's
+big screen. Phones and counters update live without reloads. Players can change
+their choice while a question is open; correctness appears only after Finish.
+Returning to the same link remembers the player. Each new game is independent
+and snapshots only the quiz's active questions.
+
+### Question timer
+
+In **Settings**, set **Timer minutes** and **Timer seconds**. Both default to 0;
+0 minutes and 0 seconds means no timer. Nonnegative whole numbers are accepted;
+extra seconds are normalized into minutes when saved. Each new game snapshots
+this setting, so editing the quiz does not disrupt a game already in progress.
+
+While a timed question is open, only the moderator's big screen shows an **M:SS**
+countdown. It starts when **Start** or **Next** opens the question, not when the
+page loads. Reloading or restarting the app keeps the original deadline.
+At zero the server automatically performs **Finish**, shows results on all
+screens, and rejects late answers. This works even without a connected big
+screen. Moderators can still **Finish** early and choose when to advance.
+
+The timer is local to this Quizzy: it is **not included in exported JSON**, and
+imported quizzes start with no timer. See [timer design notes](docs/timers.md).
+
+### Scores and prizes
+
+In **Settings**, set **Number of winners** (at least 1, default 3). Each new game
+snapshots this setting alongside the questions. Each correct final answer earns
+one point. Equal scores are ranked by the total server-measured time of correct
+answers, from question opening to the last pick. Points stay hidden during play.
+
+After **End quiz**, the big screen shows every player's place, name, and points;
+phones show their own place and points. Use **Top N** (for example, **Top 3**) to
+award prizes in leaderboard order. **Draw** guarantees prizes to players above
+the cutoff score, then draws the remaining prizes among everyone tied on that
+score, ignoring speed. Each click draws afresh and may repeat the same result.
+Players with zero points never win; if fewer than N have points, all of them win.
+**Reset winners** removes all awards. **Winner** marks and **You won!** on phones
+update live, including after reloads and reconnections.
+
+SQLite persists games, players, final choices, timings, and awards across restarts. Live presence
+uses connection tracking and short heartbeat leases for unreliable Wi-Fi; saved
+answers remain even if a player disconnects. The stage's answer counter is saved
+answers / currently connected players. All assets, QR generation, and live
+communications are local to this app.
+
+## Reuse or share a quiz
+
+Open a quiz and choose **Export**. Copy the JSON from the export page, then open
+**Import quiz** on `/moderate`, paste it into **Quiz JSON**, and choose **Import**.
+Every import creates a separate quiz, even when its title already exists. Exports
+include the title, ordered question/option contents (including inactive
+questions), and a non-default `number_of_winners` setting, not database IDs or
+runtime data. Missing `number_of_winners` defaults to 3 for older exports.
+
+`active` defaults to `true` and `correct` to `false` when omitted on import; both
+are always included in exports. Imports use the same validation as question forms:
+nonblank question text, two or more nonblank options, and at least one correct
+option. Blank option rows are skipped. Invalid input is retained with an error,
+and the entire import is rejected without saving a quiz or any questions.
+
+## Verify
+
+Dependencies have been fetched and both release and test builds work offline.
+
+```sh
+cargo test --offline
+cargo clippy --offline --all-targets -- -D warnings
+```
+
+With the app running, export the same moderator credentials, then:
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/smoke.py
+python3 tests/browser.py
+python3 tests/import_export.py
+python3 tests/import_export_browser.py
+python3 tests/live_game.py
+python3 tests/live_game_browser.py
+python3 tests/live_game_persistence.py
+python3 tests/prizes.py
+python3 tests/prizes_browser.py
+python3 tests/timer.py
+python3 tests/timer_browser.py
+python3 tests/timer_persistence.py
+```
+
+These scripts use only Python's standard library. The browser suites launch the
+installed Chromium and test the UI at desktop and phone sizes. The main browser
+suite also checks the supplied design mockups. Screenshots are saved to `storage/browser-tests/`. Set
+`QUIZZY_TEST_URL` for a server other than `http://127.0.0.1:3000`.
+
+`python3 tests/persistence.py` starts `bin/serve` on a free port and restarts it to
+verify durable data, imported contents, and deletion. Test fixtures are cleaned up automatically.
+
+See [implementation notes](docs/implementation.md) for persistence, authentication,
+validation, and preview design details.
